@startuml deployment-digitalizer-dev
!include elvira.iuml
' =============================================================================
' What: on dev the digitalizer is one namespace on control: the portal
'       (API, orchestrator) plus KEDA-scaled standalone workers (two new
'       images, and second Deployments of the ocr, analyzer, equation and image
'       images), all on Valkey db 8 (namespace shared on control); state, scans
'       and outputs stay on gateway
'       (Postgres through the k8s-bridge, the library disk over NFS), formula
'       and vision inference come from namespace shared on app01, and the
'       optional publication goes to the dev catalog. Until the services take
'       over a stage, bulk stages run in-process on low-priority workers that
'       KEDA scales to zero at peak (admission keeps their queues short).
' Kind: UML deployment diagram, instance level, proposal. Scope: data, command,
'       operator, inference and publish paths. Omitted: Loki/Mimir/Tempo
'       internals (every pod exports OTLP to its node's alloy-node), DNS, image
'       build (GHCR, CI redeploy per Deploy-a-Service), KEDA objects.
'       Implemented in this repo: deploy/k8s/base/{portal,workers,
'       priorityclasses}.yaml, deploy/k8s/overlays/dev/keda.yaml (2026-11-16).
' Source: knowledge notes NFS-Storage (written, not applied, 2026-11-12),
'         Shared-Inference (2026-11-15), Extraction-Pipeline (2026-11-14),
'         Books-Digitalizer (2026-11-08), app01 (2026-11-13), entity k8s-bridge
'         (:6432 pgbouncer, :6379 redis; kernel DNAT, no relay container per
'         STATUS 2026-11-13), entity alloy-node (OTLP/HTTP :4318), Key-Value
'         (Valkey StatefulSet on control, written, not applied, 2026-11-16);
'         this repo docs/design/deployment-restoration-studio.puml,
'         docs/design/studio-spec.md (2026-11-16).
' =============================================================================

title Books digitalizer on dev k3s: portal + kit workers on control,\ndata on gateway, inference on app01 (proposal, 2026-11-16)

node admin <<device>> [
**Operator laptop** · tailnet
----
browser: SPA (VPN only)
]

node "**gateway** · 192.168.122.227" <<virtualMachine>> as gw {
  node nfs <<executionEnvironment>> <<proposed>> [
**nfsd** (NFSv4.2) · /srv/nfs
----
raw-scans → ro
digitized → **rw** (today: ro)
]
  node bridge <<OS>> [
**k8s-bridge** · kernel DNAT (host)
:6432 PgBouncer · :6379 Redis
]
  node "**Docker Engine**" <<executionEnvironment>> as docker {
    node pg <<container>> [
**postgresql18**
db digitalizer «proposed»
]
    node redis <<container>> [
**redis** 7.4
db 7 catalog
]
  }
}

node "**control** · 192.168.122.60" <<virtualMachine>> as ct {
  frame "namespace digitalizer (proposed)" as nsd {
    node portal <<container>> <<proposed>> <<focus>> [
**digitalizer image** · default priority
----
portal: FastAPI + SPA, /metrics, /scheduler
orchestrator ×1: queue digitalizer.portal,
job_done / job_failed + beat (pump 15 s,
reconcile 60 s)
worker-interactive ×1: operator re-runs
]
    node local <<container>> <<proposed>> [
**bulk workers** (same image) · KEDA 0–N
PriorityClass digitalizer-batch (−100)
----
worker-cpu: digitalizer.cpu (clean, render)
worker-ai: digitalizer.ai (layout, formulas)
]
    node workers <<container>> <<proposed>> [
**standalone service workers** · KEDA 0–N
----
new: scan-service · render-service
same images as the catalog's, broker db 8:
ocr · analyzer · equation · image
]
    artifact pv <<proposed>> [
**PV raw-scans** (NFS, ROX)
**PV digitized** (NFS, RWX)
both under /data/library = STORAGE_PATH
**PVC scratch** (local-path)
]
  }
  frame "namespace shared" as nsct {
    node valkey <<container>> <<proposed>> [
**valkey** 9 · StatefulSet valkey-0
db 8 digitalizer dev (broker)
]
  }
  frame "namespace evilflowers-dev" as nsdev {
    node catdev <<container>> [
**evilflowers** (dev catalog)
+ analyzer · text · image · equation
]
  }
}

node "**app01** · node IP 10.99.0.7" <<device>> as app {
  frame "namespace shared" as nsshared {
    node ollama <<container>> [
**ollama** · elvira-assistant
/api/chat (vision)
]
    node vlm <<container>> <<proposed>> [
**vlm** · PaddleOCR-VL, CPU
POST /v1/formulas
]
    node laya <<container>> <<proposed>> [
**laya** · decision model
(announced; API unknown)
]
  }
}

' ---- layout only ------------------------------------------------------------------
ollama -[hidden]down- vlm
vlm -[hidden]down- laya
pv -[hidden]down- catdev
pg -[hidden]down- ollama

' ---- operator ---------------------------------------------------------------------
admin --> portal : HTTP via VPN\nREST · SSE · DZI

' ---- commands and state ------------------------------------------------------------
portal -[$accent()]-> valkey : <b>Redis protocol :6379 db 8</b>\n<b>commands + callbacks</b>
portal --> bridge : SQL :6432
workers -[$accent()]-> valkey : <b>:6379 db 8 consume,</b>\n<b>send job_done link</b>
local --> valkey : :6379 db 8 consume
local --> bridge : SQL :6432 (heartbeat)
portal --> bridge : Redis db 7 LLEN\n(backpressure, read only)
bridge --> pg : TCP
bridge --> redis : TCP

' ---- files -----------------------------------------------------------------------
workers ..> pv : <<mount>> rw
portal ..> pv : <<mount>> rw
local ..> pv : <<mount>> rw
local --> vlm : HTTP\nformula crops
pv ..> nfs : NFSv4.2 :2049\nCSI on the host

' ---- inference ---------------------------------------------------------------------
workers --> vlm : HTTP\nformula crops
workers --> laya : judges: verdicts\non uncertain items
portal --> ollama : POST /api/chat\ntitle page

' ---- publish -------------------------------------------------------------------------
portal --> catdev : optional: HTTP REST /api/v1\nentry + acquisitions
catdev --> bridge : Redis db 7\nanalyzer.extract

$legend_live_proposed()

caption Workers hold no catalog or database credential: commands and their link callbacks travel on Valkey db 8 (its own\nvisibility timeout), results as files on the library export. Until gateway exports digitized read-write over NFS,\nthe only fallback is hostPath on gateway, which competes with production for its 8 cores.
footer ELVIRA · FIIT STU · evilflowers-books-digitalizer · docs/diagrams/deployment-digitalizer-dev.puml
@enduml
